    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §1210, Tax L",
    "lawSection": "Tax Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S5118\n\nSPONSOR: HELMING\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the tax law, in relation to extending the additional one\npercent sales tax for Wayne county\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nRelates to extending the authorization for Wayne County to impose addi-\ntional rates of sales and compensating use taxes.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1. Clause 34 of subparagraph (i) of the opening paragraph of\nsection 1210 of the tax law, as amended by section 1 of item FF of\nsubpart C of part XXX of chapter 58 of the laws of 2020, is amended\n\nSection 2: Provides for an immediate effective date\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe Wayne County Board of Supervisors has requested legislation to be\nintroduced in the State Legislature to grant Wayne County the ability to\nextend the additional one percent sales and compensating use tax through\nNovember 30, 2026.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to the State.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
    "multiSponsors": {
